WEBVTT

00:00:11.030 --> 00:00:12.290
Safe! Safe!

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:15.250
All right! The bases are loaded!

00:00:16.140 --> 00:00:17.500
Taiga!

00:00:16.700 --> 00:00:17.500
Taiga!

00:00:20.570 --> 00:00:22.120
Don't worry.

00:00:22.120 --> 00:00:25.180
No matter how many innings we go, I'll throw the rest.

00:02:07.770 --> 00:02:10.810
Your foot is all right, right, Nogoro-kun?

00:02:10.810 --> 00:02:11.490
Yeah.

00:02:11.960 --> 00:02:14.480
I rested it enough on first base.

00:02:14.480 --> 00:02:17.300
The last two innings should be easy.

00:02:17.300 --> 00:02:18.330
However...

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:21.340
even if we get past this pinch, it's still tied.

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:22.380
If we get into extra innings...

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:24.000
We won't allow there to be extra innings!

00:02:24.960 --> 00:02:27.680
In the next inning, we'll show you; we'll definitely win!

00:02:29.560 --> 00:02:30.840
For Taiga...

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:34.350
I don't want to let his 120 pitches go to waste.

00:02:34.910 --> 00:02:35.950
I'm begging you.

00:02:39.350 --> 00:02:40.320
I understand.

00:02:41.020 --> 00:02:41.990
Just...

00:02:41.990 --> 00:02:43.280
I will say it again.

00:02:43.280 --> 00:02:44.720
If it seems like you're forcing yourself,

00:02:44.720 --> 00:02:46.430
I will stop the game immediately.

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:47.890
Yeah.

00:02:47.890 --> 00:02:51.370
You told the coach that, but are you really all right?

00:02:51.370 --> 00:02:51.990
What are you talking about?

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:53.610
Not "what are you talking about"!?

00:02:53.610 --> 00:02:54.930
Your foot! Your foot!

00:02:54.930 --> 00:02:57.200
It's different from fielding and hitting.

00:02:57.980 --> 00:03:01.420
I was able to practice pitching, so it'll be all right.

00:03:02.130 --> 00:03:05.800
Well, if I throw with everything I've got, I don't know what'll happen.

00:03:06.360 --> 00:03:08.460
Anyways, the bases are loaded.

00:03:08.460 --> 00:03:11.110
Make sure it's not a passed ball and catch it properly.

00:03:11.110 --> 00:03:12.770
Y-Yeah...

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:17.270
Batting fourth: catcher, Komori-kun.

00:03:19.980 --> 00:03:24.500
<i>Honda-kun coming out right now is just an unexpected accident.</i>

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:26.280
<i>The game is in our favor.</i>

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:26.940
Play!

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:30.650
<i>Watching the last game, he only has a fastball.</i>

00:03:31.300 --> 00:03:38.270
<i>On top of that, his foot injury will cause Honda-kun to not pitch his best.</i>

00:03:38.270 --> 00:03:39.580
<i>Against Honda-kun as he is now,</i>

00:03:40.230 --> 00:03:41.040
<i>I can win!</i>

00:03:50.360 --> 00:03:51.880
I-It's fast!

00:03:54.260 --> 00:03:57.310
<i>That guy... Doesn't his right foot hurt?</i>

00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:03.440
T-Time out.

00:04:07.480 --> 00:04:08.510
<i>It's fast...</i>

00:04:08.510 --> 00:04:10.130
<i>It's fast!</i>

00:04:10.130 --> 00:04:12.950
<i>There's no evidence of his foot injury!</i>

00:04:13.600 --> 00:04:16.900
<i>They're completely different from the pitches I was watching from up in the stands.</i>

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:18.320
<i>It's impossible!</i>

00:04:18.320 --> 00:04:20.660
<i>It's not a pitch I can hit.</i>

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:25.970
Excuse me.

00:04:26.570 --> 00:04:27.420
Play!

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:34.510
<i>But... it's the bottom of the eighth, two outs,
and the bases are loaded.</i>

00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:38.640
<i>If there's a way for us to capitalize on this opportunity...</i>

00:04:39.890 --> 00:04:40.890
<i>There's only this!</i>

00:04:45.140 --> 00:04:46.200
Foul!

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:50.440
<i>Komori!</i>

00:04:51.310 --> 00:04:54.380
<i>Without caring to swing, a safety bunt?</i>

00:04:54.380 --> 00:04:56.800
<i>Well, with these pitches, it's not impossible.</i>

00:05:04.680 --> 00:05:06.670
Is that fine with you, Komori?

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:11.520
Well, I'm thankful.

00:05:11.520 --> 00:05:16.130
Because I'm not scared of you at all if you don't even want to swing the bat.

00:05:17.950 --> 00:05:19.190
<i>Scared?</i>

00:05:19.190 --> 00:05:21.170
<i>Honda-kun... of me?</i>

00:05:22.030 --> 00:05:24.140
Komori! Swing!

00:05:24.140 --> 00:05:26.500
Aren't you Mifune's fourth batter?

00:05:26.500 --> 00:05:27.310
Make it a battle!

00:05:28.090 --> 00:05:31.900
Even if you swing and aren't able to hit it, no one will complain!

00:05:32.610 --> 00:05:34.110
Yamane-kun...

00:05:34.110 --> 00:05:35.530
That's right!

00:05:35.530 --> 00:05:39.350
Only you can hit Honda-kun's pitches, Komori!

00:05:39.350 --> 00:05:40.620
Oobayashi-kun...

00:05:40.620 --> 00:05:42.990
Komori!

00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:42.990
Komori, hit it!

00:05:44.220 --> 00:05:45.200
Everyone...

00:05:46.100 --> 00:05:48.080
<i>Hit it, Komori.</i>

00:06:09.190 --> 00:06:10.020
Foul!

00:06:10.020 --> 00:06:10.980
He hit it!

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:15.190
<i>T-This guy's pretty good! His timing's on!</i>

00:06:16.760 --> 00:06:18.410
<i>As expected of you, Komori.</i>

00:06:18.830 --> 00:06:20.870
<i>That look of yours...</i>

00:06:21.490 --> 00:06:22.830
<i>is more like you!</i>

00:06:25.370 --> 00:06:26.540
Foul!

00:06:27.730 --> 00:06:29.540
<i>I can hit it. I can hit it!</i>

00:06:30.220 --> 00:06:31.210
<i>Throw a ball, Shigeno.</i>

00:06:31.680 --> 00:06:34.210
<i>We've got him cornered, so stop throwing it down the middle!</i>

00:06:37.380 --> 00:06:38.690
Foul!

00:06:43.790 --> 00:06:46.550
<i>Damn. Did that guy do it on purpose!?</i>

00:06:46.550 --> 00:06:47.930
<i>I don't care what happens.</i>

00:06:49.410 --> 00:06:52.440
<i>Honda-kun has always been the person I looked up to.</i>

00:06:53.650 --> 00:06:54.480
<i>In Little League...</i>

00:06:54.730 --> 00:06:55.900
<i>In Junior High...</i>

00:06:55.900 --> 00:06:57.820
<i>Even during the Kaido exam.</i>

00:06:57.820 --> 00:07:03.080
<i>To me, Honda-kun was always a player that was on a level higher than the clouds, but...</i>

00:07:04.240 --> 00:07:06.200
<i>I will hit it!</i>

00:07:08.630 --> 00:07:11.620
<i>In order to go to Koshien with this team,</i>

00:07:12.170 --> 00:07:13.580
<i>I will, today,</i>

00:07:13.580 --> 00:07:15.250
<i>win against you!</i>

00:07:37.300 --> 00:07:39.540
Strike! Batter out!

00:07:39.540 --> 00:07:40.730
Three outs! Change!

00:07:40.730 --> 00:07:41.610
All right!

00:07:48.040 --> 00:07:50.500
<i>That last pitch was also down the middle.</i>

00:07:50.930 --> 00:07:52.300
<i>Even so,</i>

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:54.250
<i>I couldn't hit it at all.</i>

00:07:55.760 --> 00:07:58.210
<i>Honda-kun was only serious...</i>

00:07:58.210 --> 00:08:00.310
<i>for the last pitch.</i>

00:08:08.740 --> 00:08:09.890
Strike!

00:08:11.700 --> 00:08:12.620
Huh?

00:08:17.820 --> 00:08:20.110
Um, excuse me?

00:08:20.110 --> 00:08:22.030
The game between Seishuu and Mifune...

00:08:22.030 --> 00:08:23.340
Is it over already?

00:08:23.340 --> 00:08:25.650
Yeah, it's been over for a long time.

00:08:25.650 --> 00:08:29.410
Eh? W-Which team won!?

00:08:32.670 --> 00:08:35.780
But the last inning ended so quickly!

00:08:35.780 --> 00:08:39.120
I produced the winning run, huh? It feels good!

00:08:39.120 --> 00:08:43.080
The right and center fielder ran into each other, dropped the ball, and that was it.

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:46.250
Shut up. A winning run is a winning run.

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:49.840
Well, it was all thanks to Shigeno's three runs...

00:08:49.840 --> 00:08:52.490
and the fact that we had perfect relief.

00:08:53.070 --> 00:08:57.030
But it was thanks to Shimizu-kun pitching out of sticky situations up until then, wasn't it?

00:08:58.100 --> 00:09:03.000
You don't have to compliment me. I didn't do much to help...

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:04.770
That's not true.

00:09:05.760 --> 00:09:10.200
You were cool enough to be compared to darling.

00:09:14.560 --> 00:09:17.460
Tell that to my sister next time.

00:09:19.240 --> 00:09:22.340
The cheeky brat's getting embarrassed.

00:09:22.340 --> 00:09:23.500
Be quiet!

00:09:23.500 --> 00:09:28.210
He doesn't want to be told by some guy that gets in the way and is completely useless!

00:09:28.210 --> 00:09:29.520
What!?

00:09:31.450 --> 00:09:32.640
<i>Honda.</i>

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:36.480
<i>Go to Koshien. </i>

00:09:40.800 --> 00:09:42.660
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:09:46.070 --> 00:09:49.580
20 pitches, you fielded, and ran!?

00:09:50.470 --> 00:09:51.720
Well, yeah.

00:09:58.820 --> 00:10:00.870
When's your next game?

00:10:01.420 --> 00:10:03.420
I think it's in four days.

00:10:04.190 --> 00:10:06.880
You'll give me a shot again, won't you?

00:10:09.370 --> 00:10:11.930
Well, if you want to play no matter what,

00:10:11.930 --> 00:10:14.430
I wouldn't mind injecting freezing again.

00:10:14.980 --> 00:10:17.750
But you should remember this:

00:10:17.750 --> 00:10:24.260
Freezing is only there to suppress the pain. The injury itself won't get better.

00:10:24.260 --> 00:10:26.860
And, every time I inject it, the result won't be as strong.

00:10:27.510 --> 00:10:29.310
You have your future to think about.

00:10:29.310 --> 00:10:31.650
Think about it well before doing it.

00:10:33.080 --> 00:10:34.830
<i>Future, huh?</i>

00:10:35.510 --> 00:10:41.000
<i>The only thing in my future right now is to pitch my best during the Kaido game.</i>

00:10:48.900 --> 00:10:49.680
<i>Komori...</i>

00:10:52.390 --> 00:10:54.100
D-Don't tell me!

00:10:56.050 --> 00:10:59.520
W-WAIT, KOMORI!

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:01.320
Don't be rash!

00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:09.990
W-What're you doing all of a sudden!?

00:11:09.990 --> 00:11:12.820
Just because you lost during a game in high school baseball, so what!?

00:11:12.820 --> 00:11:17.620
You're still young; there're still a lot of fun things to do that'll make you feel good in life!

00:11:19.130 --> 00:11:20.330
Huh?

00:11:22.800 --> 00:11:24.170
My bad, my bad!

00:11:24.170 --> 00:11:28.050
I thought that because you were shocked you lost, you were going to do something unthinkable.

00:11:28.520 --> 00:11:32.640
Geez. What kind of misunderstanding is that?
There's no way that'd be true.

00:11:33.150 --> 00:11:37.600
Well, it's true that I was blue because we lost the game.

00:11:40.180 --> 00:11:41.560
Komori...

00:11:42.800 --> 00:11:47.520
It's okay. The reason we lost was because our team wasn't strong enough.

00:11:48.800 --> 00:11:52.570
That's what a battle is, so it can't be helped.

00:11:54.590 --> 00:11:55.280
But...

00:11:55.830 --> 00:12:00.750
I still wanted to hit Honda-kun's pitches there.

00:12:04.220 --> 00:12:05.330
Bye then.

00:12:10.530 --> 00:12:11.580
Komori!

00:12:13.330 --> 00:12:15.370
You... have a mitt, right?

00:12:17.260 --> 00:12:19.970
Will you catch my pitching one more time?

00:12:25.100 --> 00:12:25.600
Okay!

00:12:33.150 --> 00:12:34.700
Here I go, Komori!

00:12:35.320 --> 00:12:37.160
<i>Thank you, Honda-kun.</i>

00:12:56.320 --> 00:12:57.520
<i>Goodbye...</i>

00:12:59.060 --> 00:13:02.770
<i>Goodbye, my high school baseball!</i>

00:13:02.770 --> 00:13:07.770
This is a free fansub.

00:13:02.770 --> 00:13:07.770
Not for sale or rent.

00:13:10.330 --> 00:13:12.600
Still no outs with runners on first and second.

00:13:12.600 --> 00:13:15.650
Bottom of the sixth, Kawakami Jitsugyo won't stop.

00:13:16.030 --> 00:13:19.850
Batting is Niiza-kun, who already hit one home run earlier today.

00:13:19.850 --> 00:13:21.560
The pitcher delivers the second pitch...

00:13:21.560 --> 00:13:22.260
And he hits it!

00:13:22.260 --> 00:13:24.100
This is big! It's going!

00:13:24.100 --> 00:13:27.140
Left! Back! Left! Back! He sees it go!

00:13:27.140 --> 00:13:28.890
It's a home run!

00:13:28.890 --> 00:13:31.250
It's a three-run home run.

00:13:32.310 --> 00:13:34.920
This inning Kawakami Jitsugyo has scored five runs.

00:13:34.920 --> 00:13:36.340
They have the lead-

00:13:37.890 --> 00:13:40.350
This is our next opponent, Kawakami Jitsugyo.

00:13:41.270 --> 00:13:46.030
In the first and second game put together, after the other team scored 10 runs,

00:13:46.030 --> 00:13:47.810
their own team scored 30 runs; they won both games by the mercy rule.

00:13:48.230 --> 00:13:51.520
You could say they're an incredible team that hits a lot.

00:13:52.790 --> 00:13:53.730
This is bad.

00:13:53.730 --> 00:13:55.190
They're strong.

00:13:57.540 --> 00:13:59.310
It seems as though our lucky streak...

00:13:59.310 --> 00:14:01.620
ends here.

00:14:02.470 --> 00:14:08.080
Well, it'll depend on how long Shimizu-kun can keep this team down.

00:14:09.890 --> 00:14:11.410
Hey.

00:14:11.410 --> 00:14:13.840
Hey! You're late, Taiga!

00:14:13.840 --> 00:14:15.750
We said we'd watch the video today!

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:19.050
Sorry, I went to the hospital.

00:14:19.050 --> 00:14:19.680
Hospital?

00:14:20.110 --> 00:14:25.640
The place where I stopped the ball they hit... I thought that it was hurting for a while...

00:14:26.030 --> 00:14:29.600
It seems I've broken my ring finger.

00:14:32.150 --> 00:14:34.280
What!? 

00:14:40.590 --> 00:14:41.740
Are you serious?

00:14:42.170 --> 00:14:44.580
The game is cancelled because of rain?

00:14:44.580 --> 00:14:46.980
And I thought I'd come to see their ugly faces for once.

00:14:50.010 --> 00:14:52.360
If we win just two more games, it's the Kaido game, huh?

00:14:52.360 --> 00:14:55.420
I'm finally able to see them in reality.

00:14:56.120 --> 00:14:58.420
Hey, Sato! Hurry up!

00:14:58.420 --> 00:14:59.380
I'm sorry!

00:14:59.870 --> 00:15:01.840
There's no one left, right?

00:15:01.840 --> 00:15:02.480
Yes, sir.

00:15:02.480 --> 00:15:03.550
I'm the last person.

00:15:04.280 --> 00:15:05.510
<i>Toshiya?</i>

00:15:06.260 --> 00:15:07.730
Hey, Toshiya!

00:15:10.250 --> 00:15:11.390
Goro-kun.

00:15:12.750 --> 00:15:15.590
Long time no see! You look great!

00:15:15.590 --> 00:15:19.070
I heard that you'd hurt your foot, but are you all right now?

00:15:19.900 --> 00:15:22.520
Yeah, this is no big deal!

00:15:22.520 --> 00:15:24.950
And? What are you doing here today?

00:15:25.640 --> 00:15:26.950
What do you mean, "what"?

00:15:26.950 --> 00:15:29.740
I'm here to research. Research!

00:15:29.740 --> 00:15:33.460
If we win two more games, we'll meet with you guys in the semifinals, right?

00:15:34.010 --> 00:15:36.300
Really? I didn't know.

00:15:36.300 --> 00:15:37.170
You've been doing your best.

00:15:38.550 --> 00:15:39.950
Sato, we're leaving.

00:15:39.950 --> 00:15:41.260
Oh, yes!

00:15:42.080 --> 00:15:44.820
Sorry, it seems as though we're leaving.

00:15:44.820 --> 00:15:46.460
Well then, do your best.

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:00.020
W-What'd he say?

00:16:00.020 --> 00:16:01.510
W-What'd he say?

00:16:06.760 --> 00:16:08.910
It's cancelled after all...

00:16:11.390 --> 00:16:13.490
Shigeno-senpai?

00:16:16.720 --> 00:16:18.310
Shigeno-senpai!

00:16:18.310 --> 00:16:20.050
What's wrong?

00:16:20.930 --> 00:16:22.800
You'll catch a cold-

00:16:21.780 --> 00:16:23.400
You didn't know?

00:16:23.400 --> 00:16:24.180
Yes?

00:16:24.780 --> 00:16:27.340
"Do your best"?

00:16:28.480 --> 00:16:34.190
The district tournament... Us... They aren't taking any notice?

00:16:37.320 --> 00:16:38.200
Sato.

00:16:38.750 --> 00:16:41.110
Who were you talking to earlier?

00:16:41.110 --> 00:16:44.360
Oh, Goro-kun. Shigeno Goro.

00:16:45.050 --> 00:16:48.400
Shigeno? Why was he there?

00:16:48.400 --> 00:16:50.360
It seems he came to watch the game.

00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:52.950
He was saying that in three games from now, he'd be up against us.

00:16:52.950 --> 00:16:54.670
Where did Shigeno go again?

00:16:55.200 --> 00:16:58.660
If I remember correctly, a place called Seishuu, a former all-girls school.

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:00.010
Oh, that's right, that's right.

00:17:00.540 --> 00:17:04.570
And then he hurt his foot in a game against our second string or whatever?

00:17:05.500 --> 00:17:07.010
What an idiot.

00:17:07.470 --> 00:17:12.000
If he'd stayed with us, he would've gone to Koshien without a problem.

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:13.270
That's enough! Stop!

00:17:13.770 --> 00:17:16.220
Talking about a loser isn't pleasant.

00:17:28.460 --> 00:17:29.870
Hey, Goro!

00:17:30.370 --> 00:17:32.140
What time do you think it is?

00:17:32.740 --> 00:17:34.330
It'll bother the neighbors!

00:17:37.250 --> 00:17:43.590
Shut up. At 9pm nowadays, no one's asleep.

00:17:48.910 --> 00:17:50.250
<i>It's horrible, Shigeno!</i>

00:17:50.250 --> 00:17:52.140
<i>Taiga's unable to throw!</i>

00:17:52.480 --> 00:17:53.480
<i>What?</i>

00:17:54.650 --> 00:17:55.190
<i>You...</i>

00:17:55.190 --> 00:17:56.820
<i>How's your foot?</i>

00:17:57.340 --> 00:18:01.650
<i>The coach is saying he might have to think about forfeiting!</i>

00:18:03.820 --> 00:18:06.860
<i>Forfeit? You've got to be joking!</i>

00:18:06.860 --> 00:18:09.070
<i>Tell the coach not to worry about my foot!</i>

00:18:09.920 --> 00:18:13.040
<i>All I have to do is pitch the entire time, right?</i>

00:18:16.470 --> 00:18:18.310
<i>Just wait, Kaido.</i>

00:18:18.310 --> 00:18:19.650
<i>Whether you like it or not,</i>

00:18:19.650 --> 00:18:21.940
<i>I'll have you guys put me in your field of vision.</i>

00:18:27.070 --> 00:18:28.630
It's been a while...

00:18:28.630 --> 00:18:31.180
since we've gone to watch one of Goro's games.

00:18:31.180 --> 00:18:34.170
I don't really care, but stop sticking so close!

00:18:34.170 --> 00:18:35.140
It's hot.

00:18:35.490 --> 00:18:37.300
It's not something to get embarrassed over.

00:18:37.300 --> 00:18:38.320
Who is?

00:18:38.320 --> 00:18:39.470
Is that you, Shigeno?

00:18:41.870 --> 00:18:43.110
Katsuragi!

00:18:43.630 --> 00:18:44.980
It's been a while!

00:18:44.980 --> 00:18:46.430
What're you doing here?

00:18:46.430 --> 00:18:47.740
What do you mean, "what"?

00:18:47.740 --> 00:18:50.210
I'm working. It's work.

00:18:50.210 --> 00:18:52.760
I'm checking out Niiza, Kawakami Jitsugyo's fourth batter.

00:18:52.760 --> 00:18:55.070
Oh, I see.

00:18:56.250 --> 00:19:00.060
Oh, this is Katsuragi. He's the same age as I am;

00:19:00.060 --> 00:19:01.300
I used to play baseball with him.

00:19:01.300 --> 00:19:03.310
Nice to meet you, I'm Katsuragi.

00:19:03.310 --> 00:19:06.550
Right now I'm a part of the Ocean's editorial department and am working as a scout.

00:19:08.290 --> 00:19:09.020
My name is Momoko.

00:19:09.630 --> 00:19:12.520
But, what are you doing here?

00:19:12.520 --> 00:19:16.590
Taking your beautiful wife to watch baseball at noon...

00:19:16.590 --> 00:19:18.330
It's something to be jealous of.

00:19:18.330 --> 00:19:20.770
Idiot. My son's going to play.

00:19:21.350 --> 00:19:25.550
His third year and last summer. Today he's supposed to be starting,

00:19:25.550 --> 00:19:28.240
so I just came to cheer him on.

00:19:28.650 --> 00:19:30.030
Your son...

00:19:30.760 --> 00:19:33.310
Isn't he <i>that</i> Honda's only son?

00:19:33.310 --> 00:19:33.990
Yeah.

00:19:34.470 --> 00:19:37.830
Well then, we'll be cheering for him from first base,

00:19:37.830 --> 00:19:39.060
so what are you going to do?

00:19:39.060 --> 00:19:40.850
I won't do anything to interfere.

00:19:40.850 --> 00:19:43.060
That so? Bye then.

00:19:43.060 --> 00:19:44.600
Yeah, see you later.

00:19:51.780 --> 00:19:54.550
Shigeno's son, huh?

00:19:58.080 --> 00:19:59.020
That guy...

00:19:59.020 --> 00:20:02.430
He's the reliever who threw amazing pitches when he came out during the Mifune game!

00:20:02.430 --> 00:20:04.570
So he's starting today?

00:20:10.320 --> 00:20:11.240
<i>Freezing?</i>

00:20:11.800 --> 00:20:13.340
<i>Yeah.</i>

00:20:13.340 --> 00:20:16.700
<i>Last time, the reason I was able to pitch well was because of that.</i>

00:20:17.770 --> 00:20:22.030
<i>Nogoro-kun, why have you gone so far?</i>

00:20:22.030 --> 00:20:23.920
<i>Please, let me do it.</i>

00:20:24.750 --> 00:20:27.500
<i>I want to go as far as I can.</i>

00:20:28.350 --> 00:20:31.100
<i>Our dream isn't over yet.</i>

00:20:32.220 --> 00:20:35.430
<i>I can't quit at such a place.</i>

00:20:37.060 --> 00:20:38.150
<i>Nogoro-kun.</i>

00:20:39.440 --> 00:20:42.970
<i>Please forget the talk about forfeiting.</i>

00:20:45.760 --> 00:20:49.000
<i>"The boys are ambitious," right?</i>

00:20:53.040 --> 00:20:54.700
Play ball!

00:20:55.750 --> 00:20:59.660
<i>Honda's keepsake, and now he's Shigeno's son.</i>

00:21:00.190 --> 00:21:04.050
<i>If those kinds of students show any type of ability,</i>

00:21:04.050 --> 00:21:06.730
<i>the mass media will probably make a huge deal out of it.</i>

00:21:06.730 --> 00:21:11.760
<i>But if he hasn't been listed by our scouts for three years, then...</i>

00:21:22.630 --> 00:21:24.560
<i>T-This is...</i>

00:21:34.730 --> 00:21:37.220
Why are we going home so quickly!?

00:21:37.220 --> 00:21:38.620
It was a complete-game, no-hit shutout!

00:21:39.460 --> 00:21:44.160
I wanted to praise Goro, who pitched so amazingly!

00:21:44.160 --> 00:21:45.560
Don't be stupid.

00:21:45.560 --> 00:21:49.780
If we do something like that, our idiot son will become more spoiled.

00:21:49.780 --> 00:21:51.130
"Idiot son"?

00:21:51.920 --> 00:21:57.250
I'm not completely agreeing with him playing in games by using freezing.

00:21:58.310 --> 00:22:03.650
Even today, I was planning on today being his last game in high school and came to watch him.

00:22:03.650 --> 00:22:04.350
What?

00:22:04.800 --> 00:22:09.600
But then that idiot, he showed amazing results with that foot!

00:22:10.780 --> 00:22:14.440
To tell you the truth, rather than worrying about Goro's future,

00:22:15.030 --> 00:22:20.030
with his pitching today, as another baseball player, he stole my heart!

00:22:21.130 --> 00:22:24.700
I don't think anyone will be able to stop him.

00:22:24.700 --> 00:22:28.790
How far he can go in the future...

00:22:30.010 --> 00:22:31.690
We can only watch and protect.

00:22:34.690 --> 00:22:37.720
Yes, that's right! That's right, boss!

00:22:38.110 --> 00:22:40.120
He's <i>that</i> Shigeno's son.

00:22:41.950 --> 00:22:44.150
Yes, that Shigeno Goro won with a...

00:22:44.150 --> 00:22:49.190
complete-game, no-hit shutout against the incredible hitting Kawakami Jitsugyo!

00:22:49.900 --> 00:22:52.900
An amazing monster has appeared!

00:22:53.580 --> 00:22:54.930
With today's performance,

00:22:54.930 --> 00:22:57.170
I'm sure the other baseball teams will redo their lists!

00:22:58.130 --> 00:22:59.360
But, before that,

00:23:00.160 --> 00:23:06.250
we, the Yokohama Blue Oceans, should try our hardest and get him on our team!

00:24:40.450 --> 00:24:45.050
The monster battery that I've been up against before is our fourth opponent.

00:24:45.050 --> 00:24:47.640
I'll train so that I can hit that high-speed slider!

00:24:48.290 --> 00:24:52.180
Also, Ayane goes to Toshiya's side to tell him how she feels.

00:24:52.180 --> 00:24:53.640
Next time, on Major:

00:24:53.640 --> 00:24:54.850
An Unexpected Reunion.

00:24:54.850 --> 00:24:57.290
Run to the stage of your dreams!
